BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aamas-2027-deadline-abstract@scientific-conference-calendar
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20261002T115900Z
DTEND:20261002T125900Z
SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Reinforcement Learning] AAMAS 2027 - Main-track 
 abstract registration deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Autonomous Agents
  and Multiagent Systems\nWebsite: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas
 2027/\nSource URL: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/call
 -for-main-track/\nLocation: Hanoi\, Vietnam\nTopics: Machine Learning\, R
 einforcement Learning\, Autonomous Agents & Multiagent Systems\, Human-AI
  Interaction & Deployment\nSize: XL\nSubmission type: Paper-based / Blue 
 Sky Ideas short papers\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10
 -30\nNotes: Annual flagship meeting in Hanoi. New main-track submissions 
 are closed because the Oct 1 abstract gate has passed. The separate four-
 page Blue Sky Ideas track is open: its OpenReview form (opened Oct 20) wa
 s observed live on 2026-10-30\, and its Nov 5 gate only controls the Nov 
 12 short papers. A Demonstrations call posted Oct 27 (four-page paper plu
 s video\, in the proceedings\, due Dec 27 AoE) is not tracked as a separa
 te route. The AAAI fast track is limited to highly rated AAAI-27 papers a
 nd is not a general new-paper route. Size XL is an editorial estimate. Hi
 storical acceptance covers main full papers only\, not Blue Sky Ideas or 
 the newly introduced 2027 Findings track.\nScope: Autonomous agents and m
 ulti-agent systems: learning and adaptation\, coordination\, game theory\
 , planning\, reasoning\, agent engineering\, and agent-based simulation. 
 Also covers human-agent interaction\, robot teams\, norms and governance\
 , and generative agents. The contribution should concern agents or their 
 interaction\; generic language-model or learning results are not automati
 cally in scope.\nAdditional topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Probab
 ilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Control & Robotics\, Complex Systems 
 & Network Science\, Ethics & Governance\, Explainability & Interpretabili
 ty\nScope sources (2027): https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/cal
 ls/call-for-main-track/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/call-for-main-track/
END:VEVENT
